 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Complexity:** Time complexity is proportional to the number of rays and the number of voxels intersected per ray (Siddon traversal). Memory complexity depends on the partitioning mode (view or spatial) [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Complexity:** Time complexity is proportional to the number of rays and the number of voxels intersected per ray (Siddon traversal) [S1, unofficial]. Memory complexity depends on the partitioning mode (view or spatial) [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Performance:** In a 512^3 experiment, cross-node view partitioning demonstrated up to 6.74× projection speedup on eight GPUs with checked numerical parity [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Supports arbitrary trajectories, trainable geometry, and native first-order derivatives. Efficient multi-GPU execution via view and spatial partitions [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Does not integrate finite-area pixel footprints (point-ray sampling). Voxel spacing must be isotropic. Analytical methods (FBP/FDK) are restricted to fixed geometry and do not support trainable acquisition parameters [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When to use:** Differentiable iterative reconstruction with arbitrary geometry or trainable calibration parameters.
